    <string name="cert_proxy">Set WiFi proxy</string>
    <string name="cert_proxy_failed">Cannot open WiFi settings, set the proxy manually</string>
    <string name="cert_hint">1. Import the proxy CA (Burp/mitmproxy/Charles: PEM/DER/PKCS12/BKS).\n2. "Install as user certificate" needs no root, but only works for apps that trust user CAs.\n3. "Virtual app capture mode" lowers the container targetSdk to 23, so virtual apps accept user CAs with zero APK modification (no signature change, no tamper detection).\n4. With root you can install a system root CA for every app.\n5. Apps with code-level pinning or Play Integrity still need Frida (frida-gadget) or root.\nRemember to set the WiFi proxy on this device (e.g. 192.168.1.5:8080).</string>

    <string name="virtual_capture_mode">Virtual app capture mode</string>
    <string name="capture_list_hint">Enabling the mode lowers the app\'s visible targetSdk to 23 in the container so it accepts the user certificate installed above. The APK is never modified. Virtual apps must be fully stopped first, and disable the mode when you are done capturing.</string>
